    { heading: 'Why swirl marks are so visible on Piedmont cars', body: [
      'Swirl marks are fine scratches in the clear coat, and they show worst on exactly the colours that are common here — black, dark grey, deep blue and metallic silver on well-kept cars. They come from washing, not from driving: automatic brush washes, dirty wash mitts, and drying with a towel that picked up grit last time.',
